The module compiles cleanly. It uses a `negedge clk` triggered always block with the reset checked synchronously inside the block, loading `8'h34` when `reset` is asserted.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input clk,
    input reset,
    input [7:0] d,
    output reg [7:0] q
);

    always @(negedge clk) begin
        if (reset)
            q <= 8'h34;
        else
            q <= d;
    end

endmodule
```
